# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile ENTRYPOINT boots MinIO in the background, creates `testbucket`
# with an anonymous *download* policy (the vulnerability), and then execs
# `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * MinIO is ALREADY RUNNING with the public bucket when the agent starts;
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so restarting MinIO cannot kill the container.
#
# The bucket policy is server-side state re-evaluated per request, so the fix
# (`mc anonymous set none`) takes effect live and needs no MinIO restart.
